{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And I turned.</b> The matter: I engaged in wisdom and in merriment, which is wine, for he who drinks of it becomes merrily delirious and goes mad; and folly is building and acquiring wealth." "<b>For what is the man.</b> Like the matter of (Psalms 144:3), 'what is man that You should know him,' and likewise, 'what is man that You should remember him.' The matter: when I saw my heavens and moon and stars, and that the world stands as though under one star, I said, 'what is man that You should remember him,' and You made for him greatness and surpassing elevation. And the matter: 'for what capacity can there be in a man who comes after the king, and all that he does — others have already done it.' And the word 'the doers' is missing, like (Genesis 41:55) 'and he said to Joseph' — without mentioning there the one who says; and likewise (Exodus 2:22) 'who bore her to Levi,' and many like these. Some say that 'the king' is from 'and my heart reigned over me,' and the matter is: what is the point and the response that can come after the counsel, and pursue all that the ancients did — and this is not correct."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:16.589526599Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}